# Architectural invariants

Read `AGENTS.md` first. These rules are not negotiable:

1. **Zero AI at run-time.** No LLM SDK imports, dynamic prompts or agent logic in production extractors, Airflow
   DAGs or dbt models. AI only generates deterministic artifacts at design-time. `python/tests/test_no_llm_at_runtime.py`
   enforces this.
2. **Single source of contracts.** Schemas, validation rules and mappings live in this
   repository (`configs/contracts/`, `configs/ingestions/`) and nowhere else. Everything runs on this machine.
3. **Obscura.** Browser-based probes and extractors use `playwright` through `scrapagents.stealth.StealthRouter`,
   which connects to Obscura (`obscura.sh`, a headless browser in Rust) over CDP (`OBSCURA_CDP_URL`). Do not
   launch a local Chromium elsewhere. Obscura does not replace the legal review: report blocks and ToS, never
   work around them without an H1 decision.
4. **Stream-to-Rust.** Python extractors stream bytes to `SourceRuntime` (Rust). Every payload is
   written to RustFS first (structured and binary). Only PDF/DOCX then go through Apache Tika, and
   the extracted text is written back to RustFS. PostgreSQL `bronze` is loaded by reading the
   object back from RustFS. JSON, XML, HTML and CSV never touch Tika.
5. **HITL gates.** Humans own Macro-H1, Producto OI value, and PR merge; `gate-sentinel` may
   auto-sign green H1/H2 only (see `human-gates.mdc`).
